# The game's site blocks — the tenant fragment (hub contract §A.3; the
# WorldConsole repo's hub/02-wiring-workflow.md, landed at H1a step 2).
# This file is the OWNING HOME of GameMaster Bernd's doors; the hub box
# carries a derived copy at
# /home/deploy/world-console/deploy/host/caddy/sites/gamemaster-bernd.caddy
# (landed by cp — contract §B step 4 — and re-landed whenever this file
# changes; then in-container `caddy validate`, then reload, NEVER the
# other order). No global options block here: the ingress Caddyfile owns
# email/ACME, and a second one would collide (§A.3). The apex
# (worldconsole.eu) is the hub's own block, not ours — the game's landing
# is play.'s by-invitation 404 by design, and the game's public
# disclosures (privacy note, Impressum) are the apex pages: the game's
# own words, moved home with the split.
#
# `import friends/*.caddy` resolves RELATIVE TO THIS FILE'S LOCATION. On
# the hub box that is sites/friends/<name>.caddy — the box-local doors,
# cp'd there from this repo's deploy/host/caddy/friends/ authoring lane
# (new-friend.sh prints the exact steps at mint). The hub tracks
# sites/friends/.keep.caddy so the glob is never empty.

play.worldconsole.eu {
	encode zstd gzip

	# Friends' doors: one box-local snippet each, minted by new-friend.sh
	# — secret path, basic auth, the friend's container + the waker as
	# second upstream. Never tracked, in this repo or the hub's.
	import friends/*.caddy

	# Unmatched paths, including / — there is no directory of doors.
	handle {
		respond "GameMaster Bernd — by invitation." 404
	}
}

# R11's isolated credential origin: reserved from day one, served only when
# the vault round builds it. Nothing else may ever share this origin.
vault.worldconsole.eu {
	respond "not yet" 404
}
